er is told that it cannot be reclaimed for that day without administrator intervention; the claim remains in force.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A dedicated parking holder can select one or more dates in the calendar up to 30 days ahead and schedule release of their assigned parking for those dates; the scheduled releases are shown on the calendar and become available for claiming at the applicable release time.\",\n     \"1: The system rejects dates outside the allowed 30-day window and prevents employees without dedicated parking from scheduling releases.\",\n     \"2: The holder can cancel a scheduled release while it remains unclaimed; the cancellation is reflected on the calendar and the space is no longer offered for that date.\",\n     \"3: If a scheduled release has already been claimed, cancellation is rejected and the holder is informed that administrator intervention is required to revert it.\",\n     \"4: The system records each scheduled release and cancellation in an audit history.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: An employee without dedicated parking can view the number of parking spaces currently available to claim; dedicated parking holders cannot claim released spaces as temporary parking.\",\n     \"1: Eligible employees receive an in-app notice or email when spaces become available; the responsive web app displays availability and allows a claim without relying on native push notifications.\",\n     \"2: Pre-scheduled releases and same-day releases made before the configured Daily Parking Release Time become available at that time (default 8:00 AM); same-day releases made after that time become available immediately.\",\n     \"3: An eligible employee can claim an available space on a first-come, first-served basis. The system atomically assigns one available space, updates the available count and records the date, time, employee, and assigned parking; t