ng administrator can configure the report's designated stakeholders; report generation and delivery do not apply warnings, suspensions, or penalties to employees in Phase 1.\",\n     \"5: If entry records are absent, the applicable unused-parking event is recorded rather than treated as confirmed use.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 3,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Folio3 Google Workspace authentication is required; dedicated-holder data is imported from the employee record, while employees without dedicated parking register at least one vehicle on first use.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: An employee signs in with a Folio3 Google Workspace account; the system authenticates the account and uses the corporate email to identify the employee and retrieve their employee profile.\",\n     \"1: A personal Gmail account, another email provider, or an account not authorized as a Folio3 employee is refused access and shown an authentication/access error.\",\n     \"2: For an employee with dedicated parking, the system populates the profile with available employee ID, name, assigned-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details, including one or more license plates and any stored make, model, or color.\",\n     \"3: On first use, an employee without dedicated parking is prompted to register at least one license plate before proceeding; make, model, and color may also be entered. The system saves the vehicle details for later parking requests.\",\n     \"4: A user with a returning profile who signs in successfully is taken to the dashboard without repeating first-use vehicle registration.\",\n     \"5: The employee accesses the same responsive web application from a phone, tablet, or desktop browser; phone controls are touch-sized. No native-app-only sign-in flow is required.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"A holder releases the assigned space for the current day; a